{% comment %}
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  VELLUTO — PDP Kit Switcher (TEST)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Daily-Elements-style bundle switcher rendered directly on the product page:
  one selectable card per kit (Starter / Performance / Ultimate), shown above
  the buy buttons. Since each kit×color is its own product (same architecture
  as the existing color switcher), the cards are plain links to the sibling
  kit product in the SAME color — no JS, crawlable, progressive.

  Driven entirely by product metafields (namespace `velluto`) — nothing is
  hardcoded, and the snippet renders NOTHING when the metafields are absent,
  so it is safe inside the shared product template:
    - kit_siblings  (single line text)  comma-separated handles of this
      color's kit versions, in display order, e.g.
      "velluto-stradapro-cycling-glasses-nero,velluto-stradapro-performance-kit-nero,velluto-stradapro-ultimate-kit-nero"
    - kit_label     (single line text)  e.g. "Performance Kit"
                    (fallback: middle segment of "… | Performance Kit | Nero")
    - kit_tagline   (single line text)  one-liner under the kit name
    - kit_badge     (single line text)  e.g. "Most Popular" — set only on the
                    recommended kit

  Usage: Custom Liquid block in the product-info section:
    {% raw %}{% render 'velluto-kit-switcher', product: product %}{% endraw %}

  Note: `all_products` only resolves ACTIVE products — draft kit products
  silently drop out of the switcher.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign kit_handles = product.metafields.velluto.kit_siblings.value | default: ''
-%}

{%- if kit_handles != blank -%}
  {{ 'velluto-kit-switcher.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  <div class="vkit">
    <p class="vkit__label">Choose your kit</p>
    <div class="vkit__list">
      {%- assign handles = kit_handles | split: ',' -%}
      {%- for h in handles -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign kit_handle = h | strip
          assign kit_product = all_products[kit_handle]
          if kit_product == blank
            continue
          endif

          assign title_parts = kit_product.title | split: '|'
          if title_parts.size > 1
            assign fallback_label = title_parts[1] | strip
          else
            assign fallback_label = kit_product.title
          endif
          assign kit_label = kit_product.metafields.velluto.kit_label.value | default: fallback_label
          assign kit_tagline = kit_product.metafields.velluto.kit_tagline.value
          assign kit_badge = kit_product.metafields.velluto.kit_badge.value
          assign is_current = false
          if kit_product.handle == product.handle
            assign is_current = true
          endif
        -%}
        <a
          href="{{ kit_product.url }}"
          class="vkit__card{% if is_current %} is-active{% endif %}"
          {% if is_current %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}
        >
          <span class="vkit__radio" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="vkit__main">
            <span class="vkit__name">
              {{ kit_label }}
              {%- if kit_badge != blank %}<span class="vkit__badge">{{ kit_badge }}</span>{% endif -%}
            </span>
            {%- if kit_tagline != blank -%}
              <span class="vkit__tagline">{{ kit_tagline }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
          <span class="vkit__pricing">
            <span class="vkit__price">{{ kit_product.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
            {%- comment -%}
              Value framing, not discount framing — the compare-at price is
              shown as the value of the individual items.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if kit_product.compare_at_price > kit_product.price -%}
              <span class="vkit__value">{{ kit_product.compare_at_price | money_without_trailing_zeros }} value</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
        </a>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
